From 37ff3948e974540d90375c5a9fd41c11e183f76d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amit Kumar <amit@example.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:00:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 09: Knowledge Distillation + live two-stage unlearning
 animation (Page 6)

- core/unlearning/knowledge_distillation.py: run_knowledge_distillation,
  Hinton-style KD (alpha*CE + (1-alpha)*T^2*KL) distilling the pre-ascent
  global model back into the post-ascent model, trained only on retained
  clients; tracks per-retained-client accuracy before/after.
- core/unlearning/unlearning_engine.py: start_unlearning now chains
  Gradient Ascent -> Knowledge Distillation, capturing the pre-ascent
  checkpoint as KD's teacher before it's overwritten, with per-stage
  status persistence.
- core/unlearning/storage.py: save_final_checkpoint/load_final_checkpoint
  for the fully-unlearned model (unlearning_final_model.pt).
- core/unlearning/cli.py, backend/src/routes/unlearning.js: pass through
  kd_epochs/kd_lr/kd_temperature/kd_alpha/kd_batch_size.
- Frontend: Page 6 built out in full -- UnlearningStepper,
  GradientAscentPanel, KnowledgeDistillationPanel, ClientInfluenceBars,
  and Unlearning.jsx wired to replay the real backend history
  progressively (same strategy Phase 06 established for FL), never a
  fabricated timer.
- tests/test_unlearning.py: unit tests for run_knowledge_distillation
  (including a tuned scenario proving retained accuracy measurably
  recovers), a synthetic (no-download) full start_unlearning pipeline
  test, and updated the MNIST end-to-end integration test for the new
  nested gradient_ascent/knowledge_distillation status shape.

Verified: pytest tests/ -m "not slow" (37 passed), npm run build
(frontend), node --check (backend), python -m py_compile.
